module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionRingVeroneseChart.Generation
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionRingProjImmersion.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.ProjChartGluing

/-!
# Stacks Tag 01N8 at the section ring of an ample module: `f^*𝒪_Y(d) ≅ 𝓛^{⊗ d}`

Let `X` be a scheme, `𝓛` an ample invertible `𝒪_X`-module, `S = Γ_*(X, 𝓛)` the graded section
ring of Stacks Tag 01CV, `Y = Proj S` and `f : X ⟶ Y` the canonical morphism of Stacks Tag 01PZ.
For a degree `d > 0` in which the powers of `𝓛` are generated by global sections, Stacks Tag 01N8
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.existsUnique_pair`) applied to the section
ring's own Veronese datum `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartFromRatios.sectionRingVeronese`
produces a **unique** pair

`(φ : X ⟶ U_d, α : φ^*𝒪_{U_d}(d) ≅ 𝓛^{⊗ d})`

compatible with that datum. This file identifies `φ` with the canonical morphism — precisely, with
its lift `Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart.degreeLift` through `U_d` — and so reads `α` as an
isomorphism

`f^*𝒪_Y(d) ≅ 𝓛^{⊗ d}`.

**The isomorphism is not chosen.** It is the second component of the pair that Tag 01N8 proves
unique, and the normalisation that pins it is recorded as `pair_snd_hom_app_top`: it carries the
pulled-back degree-`d` section of a homogeneous `g ∈ S_d` to the global section `ψ(g)` of
`𝓛^{⊗ d}` that `g` *is*. Nothing is declared on a chart, and in particular no trivializing
generator is sent to a trivializing generator by fiat.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart.pair` — the compatible pair of Stacks Tag 01N8 at the section
  ring's Veronese datum in degree `d`.
* `Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart.twistIso` — **`f^*𝒪_Y(d) ≅ 𝓛^{⊗ d}`**, the pair's second
  component read along `pair_fst_eq_degreeLift`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart.pair_fst_eq_degreeLift` — **the morphism Stacks Tag 01N8
  produces is the canonical morphism of Stacks Tag 01PZ.** This is the uniqueness half of Tag
  01N8 used as a lever: both morphisms have the same preimage of each standard open `D₊(g)`, and
  on the fractions `a/g^n` they induce the same ring map, so
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSectionsUnique.eq_of_appLE_eq_on_away` identifies them.
* `Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart.pair_snd_hom_app_top` — the normalisation of `α`.

## The route of `pair_fst_eq_degreeLift`

The common preimage family is `chartOpen`, the preimage of `D₊(g)` under the canonical morphism,
which by clause (1) of Tag 01PZ is the nonvanishing open `X_a` of the homogeneous piece `a`
underlying `g`. For the pair's morphism that it is the preimage is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.preimage_basicOpen_eq`, a consequence of
compatibility; for the canonical morphism it is the definition.

On the fractions the two ring maps are compared through the chart. For the pair's morphism the
value of `φ^♯(a/g^n)` is characterised by the degree-`n` clause of compatibility, the local
identity `ψ(a)|_V = φ^♯(a/g^n) · ψ(g)^n|_V`. For the canonical morphism the same characterisation
holds with `φ^♯` replaced by the chart's ring map, because
* the canonical morphism restricted to `X_a` **is** Tag 01N8's chart at `a` for this datum — that
  is `Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart.chartToProj_eq_chartHom` together with
  `Stacks.SectionRingProjImmersion.ι_comp_projHomOfIsAmple`, and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.homOfLE_chartToProj` restricts that identity
  from `X_a` to the smaller open;
* so `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartGluing.appLE_awayToSection` computes `φ^♯` on `a/g^n` as
  the chart's ring map there, and
  `…ProjChartFromRatios.VeroneseSections.resTop_eq_lift_smul` is the local identity for it.

Since `ψ(g)^n` is nonvanishing on the open, the two values agree
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSectionsUnique.eq_of_smul_restrict_eq`).

## Implementation notes

**Homogeneous elements of `S_d` are destructured, never coerced.** `S_d` is the range of
`DirectSum.of _ d`, so every `g : S_d` is `DirectSum.of _ d a` for a section `a` of `𝓛^{⊗ d}`;
`exists_eq_of` performs that replacement once per proof obligation, which is what lets the
statements about `X_a` — clause (1) of Tag 01PZ, the two charts being one chart — apply at all.
The two spellings of the membership proof, `g.2` and
`Stacks.ExternalGrading.of_mem_summand d a`, are the same by proof irrelevance and no transport
appears.

**The opens are never rewritten inside `appLE`.** `chartOpen` is only ever compared with `X_a` by
an inequality, and the chart identity it needs is produced at `chartOpen` itself by restricting
the one at `X_a` along `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.homOfLE_ι`. Rewriting an open underneath
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.appLE`, whose proof argument mentions it, is what this avoids.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N5)

## What is not done here

**No degree is reached other than `d`.** The isomorphism built here is the degree-`d` one, for a
degree in which the powers of `𝓛` are globally generated; cancelling two consecutive such degrees
down to degree one is the sibling
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/SectionRingVeroneseChart/DegreeOne.lean`.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite MonoidalCategory
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj (twistingSheaf)
open HomogeneousLocalization
open Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance (grading nvOpen)
open Stacks.GradedSections (powSections sectionRing)
open Stacks.NonvanishingOpen (nonvanishingOpen)
open Stacks.TensorPowerTrivialize (resTop)
open Stacks.TensorPowers (natTensorPow)
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartFromRatios
open AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (degreeOpen)
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj (toProj pullbackTwist)
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartAlphaInstance (pullbackDegreeSection)
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal (psiSection IsCompatible)

universe u

namespace Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart

section Monoidal

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.symmetricCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isMonoidal_localIso
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isLocalization_sheafify Stacks.SheafInternalHom.monoidalCategory
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.sheafifyMonoidal Stacks.SheafInternalHom.braidedCategory
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeBraidedCategory
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemePreadditive
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeTensorRightAdditive

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (L : X.Modules) [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L]

/-! ### Homogeneous elements of the section ring in a fixed degree -/

omit [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] in
/-- **Every homogeneous element of degree `d` of the section ring is `DirectSum.of _ d a` for a
global section `a` of `L ^⊗ d`.** The degree-`d` piece is by definition the range of
`DirectSum.of _ d`, so this is destructuring rather than a theorem; it is stated in the bundled
form because every statement below needs the replacement performed before the statements about
`X_a` apply. -/
theorem exists_eq_of {d : ℕ} (g : grading L d) :
    ∃ a : powSections L d, g = ⟨DirectSum.of (powSections L) d a,
      Stacks.ExternalGrading.of_mem_summand d a⟩ := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := g.2
  exact ⟨a, Subtype.ext ha.symm⟩

/-! ### The common preimage family -/

/-- **The preimage of the standard open `D₊(g)` under the canonical morphism of Stacks Tag
01PZ**, for `g` homogeneous of degree `d`. This is the family `W` that the uniqueness engine of
Stacks Tag 01N8 compares two morphisms over. -/
def chartOpen (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) {d : ℕ} (g : grading L d) : X.Opens :=
  Stacks.SectionRingProjMorphism.projHomOfIsAmple L hL ⁻¹ᵁ
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen (grading L) (g : sectionRing L)

/-- **`chartOpen` at `DirectSum.of _ d a` is `X_a`.** Clause (1) of Stacks Tag 01PZ. -/
theorem chartOpen_of (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (a : powSections L d) :
    chartOpen L hL ⟨DirectSum.of (powSections L) d a,
        Stacks.ExternalGrading.of_mem_summand d a⟩ = nvOpen L a :=
  Stacks.SectionRingProjMorphism.projHomOfIsAmple_preimage_projBasicOpen L hL a hd

/-- **`chartOpen` is the nonvanishing open of `ψ(g)` for the section ring's Veronese datum.**
`chartOpen_of` on one side and `nonvanishingOpen_pow` in degree one on the other, the two being
`X_a` and `X_{a¹}`. -/
theorem chartOpen_eq_nonvanishingOpen_psiSection (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) {d : ℕ}
    (hd : 0 < d) (g : grading L d) :
    chartOpen L hL g
      = nonvanishingOpen X (natTensorPow L d)
          (psiSection (grading L) (sectionRingVeronese L d) g) := by
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := exists_eq_of L g
  have h1 : nvOpen L (Stacks.SectionExtension.powSec L a 1) = nvOpen L a :=
    Opens.ext (by
      rw [Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance.coe_nvOpen, Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance.coe_nvOpen,
        Stacks.SectionExtension.nvLocus_powSec_one])
  rw [chartOpen_of L hL hd a,
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.nonvanishingOpen_psiSection (grading L)
      (sectionRingVeronese L d), nonvanishingOpen_pow, h1]

/-! ### The pair of Stacks Tag 01N8 -/

/-- **The compatible pair of Stacks Tag 01N8** at the section ring's Veronese datum in degree
`d`, for a degree in which the opens `X_a`, `a ∈ Γ(X, L ^⊗ d)`, cover `X`. The pair exists and is
unique by `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.existsUnique_pair`, whose generation
hypothesis is `iSup_nonvanishingOpen_psiSection_eq_top`. -/
def pair {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d) (hcov : (⨆ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a) = ⊤) :
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSectionsUnique.Pair (grading L) (natTensorPow L d) d :=
  (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.existsUnique_pair (grading L) hd
    (sectionRingVeronese L d) (iSup_nonvanishingOpen_psiSection_eq_top L d hcov)).choose

/-- The pair of Stacks Tag 01N8 is compatible with the datum it was produced from. -/
theorem isCompatible_pair {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcov : (⨆ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a) = ⊤) :
    IsCompatible (grading L) (sectionRingVeronese L d) (pair L hd hcov) :=
  (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.existsUnique_pair (grading L) hd
    (sectionRingVeronese L d) (iSup_nonvanishingOpen_psiSection_eq_top L d hcov)).choose_spec.1

/-- The preimage of `D₊(g)` under the pair's morphism is `chartOpen`. This is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.preimage_basicOpen_eq`, which is a consequence
of compatibility and not a further hypothesis. -/
theorem preimage_basicOpen_pair (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcov : (⨆ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a) = ⊤) (g : grading L d) :
    toProj (grading L) (pair L hd hcov).1
        ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen (grading L) (g : sectionRing L)
      = chartOpen L hL g := by
  rw [Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.preimage_basicOpen_eq (grading L)
      (isCompatible_pair L hd hcov) g,
    chartOpen_eq_nonvanishingOpen_psiSection L hL hd g]

/-- The preimage of `D₊(g)` under the lift of the canonical morphism is `chartOpen`, by
definition of `chartOpen` once the lift is read back as a morphism into `Proj S`. -/
theorem preimage_basicOpen_degreeLift (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcov : (⨆ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a) = ⊤) (g : grading L d) :
    toProj (grading L) (degreeLift L hL hd hcov)
        ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen (grading L) (g : sectionRing L)
      = chartOpen L hL g := by
  rw [chartOpen, toProj_degreeLift]

/-! ### The morphism of Stacks Tag 01N8 is the canonical morphism -/

/-- **The morphism Stacks Tag 01N8 produces at the section ring's Veronese datum is the canonical
morphism of Stacks Tag 01PZ**, lifted through `U_d`.

Both have `chartOpen g` as the preimage of `D₊(g)`, and on the fractions `a/g^n` they induce the
same ring map: for the pair that value satisfies the local identity
`ψ(a)|_V = φ^♯(a/g^n) · ψ(g)^n|_V` by the degree-`n` clause of compatibility, and for the
canonical morphism the chart's ring map satisfies it, because the canonical morphism restricted to
`X_a` is the chart (`chartToProj_eq_chartHom`,
`Stacks.SectionRingProjImmersion.ι_comp_projHomOfIsAmple`) and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartGluing.appLE_awayToSection` reads the ring map off it. Since
`ψ(g)^n` is nonvanishing there the two values agree. -/
theorem pair_fst_eq_degreeLift (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcov : (⨆ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a) = ⊤) :
    (pair L hd hcov).1 = degreeLift L hL hd hcov := by
  refine Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSectionsUnique.eq_of_appLE_eq_on_away (grading L) hd
    (W := chartOpen L hL) (preimage_basicOpen_pair L hL hd hcov)
    (preimage_basicOpen_degreeLift L hL hd hcov) ?_
  intro g₀ n x hx
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := exists_eq_of L g₀
  have hmem : x ∈ grading L (n * d) := by simpa [smul_eq_mul] using hx
  set hf := Stacks.ExternalGrading.of_mem_summand d a with hfdef
  set g : grading L d := ⟨DirectSum.of (powSections L) d a, hf⟩ with hgdef
  -- the chart open and the two inequalities it satisfies
  have hVW : chartOpen L hL g ≤ nvOpen L a := le_of_eq (chartOpen_of L hL hd a)
  have hW₀ : nvOpen L a ≤ nonvanishingOpen X (natTensorPow (natTensorPow L d) 1)
      ((sectionRingVeronese L d).pow hf 1) :=
    le_nonvanishingOpen_pow_one L d a (le_refl (nvOpen L a))
  have hVle : chartOpen L hL g ≤ nonvanishingOpen X (natTensorPow (natTensorPow L d) 1)
      ((sectionRingVeronese L d).pow hf 1) := hVW.trans hW₀
  -- the canonical morphism restricted to the chart open is Tag 01N8's chart at `a`
  have hΦ : (chartOpen L hL g).ι ≫ toProj (grading L) (degreeLift L hL hd hcov)
      = ((sectionRingVeronese L d).homogeneousRatios hf hVle).chartToProj hd := by
    rw [← X.homOfLE_ι hVW, Category.assoc, toProj_degreeLift,
      Stacks.SectionRingProjImmersion.ι_comp_projHomOfIsAmple L hL a hd,
      ← chartToProj_eq_chartHom L d a hd,
      Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.homOfLE_chartToProj (grading L)
        (sectionRingVeronese L d) hf hd hW₀ hVW]
  -- the value of the canonical morphism's ring map on the fraction
  have h2 := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartGluing.appLE_awayToSection
    ((sectionRingVeronese L d).homogeneousRatios hf hVle) hd hΦ
    (preimage_basicOpen_degreeLift L hL hd hcov g).ge
    (Away.mk (grading L) hf n x hx)
  -- the local identity for the pair and for the chart
  have h1 := (isCompatible_pair L hd hcov).2 g (chartOpen L hL g)
    (preimage_basicOpen_pair L hL hd hcov g).ge n x hx ⟨x, hmem⟩ rfl
  have h3 := (sectionRingVeronese L d).resTop_eq_lift_smul hf hVle hd n x hx ⟨x, hmem⟩ rfl
  refine Eq.trans ?_ h2.symm
  exact Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSectionsUnique.eq_of_smul_restrict_eq
    (natTensorPow (natTensorPow L d) n) ((sectionRingVeronese L d).pow hf n)
    (hVle.trans ((sectionRingVeronese L d).le_nonvanishingOpen_pow hf n)) h1 h3

/-! ### The isomorphism `f^*𝒪_Y(d) ≅ 𝓛^{⊗ d}` -/

/-- The pair's morphism, read back as a morphism into `Proj S`, is the canonical morphism of
Stacks Tag 01PZ. -/
theorem toProj_pair_fst (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcov : (⨆ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a) = ⊤) :
    toProj (grading L) (pair L hd hcov).1
      = Stacks.SectionRingProjMorphism.projHomOfIsAmple L hL := by
  rw [pair_fst_eq_degreeLift L hL hd hcov, toProj_degreeLift]

/-- **`f^*𝒪_Y(d) ≅ 𝓛^{⊗ d}`**, for a degree `d > 0` in which the powers of `𝓛` are generated by
global sections. This is the second component `α` of the unique pair of Stacks Tag 01N8, read
along `toProj_pair_fst`: the pullback the pair is stated at is the pullback along the canonical
morphism of Stacks Tag 01PZ. -/
def twistIso (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcov : (⨆ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a) = ⊤) :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback (Stacks.SectionRingProjMorphism.projHomOfIsAmple L hL)).obj
        (twistingSheaf (grading L) (d : ℤ))
      ≅ natTensorPow L d :=
  eqToIso (congrArg
      (fun φ : X ⟶ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (grading L) =>
        (Scheme.Modules.pullback φ).obj (twistingSheaf (grading L) (d : ℤ)))
      (toProj_pair_fst L hL hd hcov).symm) ≪≫
    (pair L hd hcov).2

/-- **The normalisation that pins `α`.** The isomorphism carries the pulled-back degree-`d`
section of a homogeneous `g ∈ S_d` to the global section `ψ(g)` of `𝓛^{⊗ d}` that `g` is. This is
the degree-one clause of compatibility, through
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.app_top_pullbackDegreeSection`, and it is what
makes `twistIso` *the* comparison rather than some isomorphism of the two sides. -/
theorem pair_snd_hom_app_top {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcov : (⨆ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a) = ⊤) (g : grading L d) :
    (pair L hd hcov).2.hom.app ⊤
        (pullbackDegreeSection (grading L) (pair L hd hcov).1 g)
      = psiSection (grading L) (sectionRingVeronese L d) g :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.app_top_pullbackDegreeSection (grading L)
    (isCompatible_pair L hd hcov) g

end Monoidal

end Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart

end
